Fixed :meth:`vCalAddress.to_xcal() <icalendar.prop.cal_address.vCalAddress.to_xcal>` writing characters that are not allowed in XML, such as a C0 control character in an ``ORGANIZER`` or ``SENT-BY`` value parsed from jCal, which made :meth:`Component.to_xcal() <icalendar.cal.component.Component.to_xcal>` produce XML that is not well-formed. The value now goes through the same filter as the text and URI types, and that filter also removes U+FFFE and U+FFFF. I used AI (Claude Opus 5.5, via Claude Code) to find this bug, write the fix, and write its tests; I reviewed and validated the output. @alhudz
